                                        "sense_id": "473a8b85-ddea-3279-9c3b-3bf891d25064",
                                        "entry_id": "c6bc362f-c33c-32e4-886d-8671af500a45",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, from, or pertaining to Senegal or the Senegalese people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Senegalese",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a2b150a-33bd-3e0a-8b79-692fcd87ab8e",
                                        "entry_id": "826dc43f-c4f7-3ce4-985d-bb65e0076218",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person from Senegal or of Senegalese descent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80b97caf-4716-48bd-8706-320ea3720165",
                                                "sense_id": "2a2b150a-33bd-3e0a-8b79-692fcd87ab8e",
                                                "text": "Foreigner who marries a Senegalese is granted permanent residency and can apply for citizenship by naturalization."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d4620b2-c9a4-4293-a2ea-118880ed8f21",
                                                "sense_id": "2a2b150a-33bd-3e0a-8b79-692fcd87ab8e",
                                                "text": "In times of need, it is the mother's brother whom a Senegalese is most likely to approach for aid. The matrilineage is dominated by the tokor (\"tuh-CORE\"), the oldest man. The tokor holds all the family money."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3865953c-c2ed-4264-87c6-312c1a90828c",
                                                "sense_id": "2a2b150a-33bd-3e0a-8b79-692fcd87ab8e",
                                                "text": "Senghor writes that these texts were collected “by the Abbé Boilat, a Senegalese” in his Grammar of the Wolof Language. Identifying Boilat as “a Senegalese” conflicts with the more ambiguous ways that Boilat actually presents himself[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6acaef48-fea8-413c-8dcb-509062891415",
                        "source_entry_id": "4b51d6fe-0b15-33c9-8ff5-8945b6d5fb5a",
                        "source_sense_id": "42490882-7564-31f7-86b5-047aca8805a6",
